The attached image (Figure 10) illustrates the local inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 at the injection site in skeletal muscle 24 hours post-injection. The top row, showing Nano-11 co-formulated with OVA, reveals significant recruitment of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages and MHCII+ cells. Arrows point to cells with intracellular Nano-11 (red), indicating efficient uptake. In contrast, the bottom row, with soluble OVA alone, shows minimal inflammatory cell presence. This demonstrates that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response, recruiting immune cells, primarily monocytes/macrophages, which then internalize the nanoparticles, as discussed in section 3.6 of the PDF.